# mjpeg_enc — baseline JPEG, towards Motion JPEG.
#
# **Not finished.** What exists is `jpeg_fdct`, the 8x8 forward
# discrete cosine transform of ITU T.81 §A.3.3 with the level shift of
# §A.3.1. Still to come: quantisation and the zig-zag of §A.3.6, the
# entropy coder of §F.1.2 with Annex K's tables, the colour transform,
# and the framing that turns a block stream into a file. The version is
# 0.1.0 and the `top` will become `mjpeg_enc` when there is one.
#
# The transform is **not bit-exact against any other implementation and
# cannot be**: T.81 defines it mathematically and leaves the arithmetic
# to the implementer, so there is no reference bitstream to compare
# against. `ip/video/mjpeg_enc/README.md` says what is checked instead
# and gives the measured distance from a double-precision transform.
name mjpeg_enc
version 0.1.0
license MIT
description "Baseline JPEG, in progress: the 8x8 forward DCT of T.81 A.3.3 in fixed point, with the level shift, measured against a double-precision transform"

top jpeg_fdct
target ice40
target ecp5
target xc7

source rtl/jpeg_fdct.v
source rtl/jpeg_quant.v

port clk in
port rst_n in
port in_sample in 8
port in_valid in
port in_ready out
port out_coef out 12
port out_valid out
port out_ready in
